          %h2#statement_and_proof Statement and proof
          %p
            There are a number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} categorically-flavored
            ways of characterizing
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces"} compact spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relational+beta-modules"} relational beta-modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            where the beta-module structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo :
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↛
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi: \beta(X) \nrightarrow X
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+relation"} entire relation
            (satisfies
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ∘
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{\beta(X)} \leq \xi^\circ \xi
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact space
          #char.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              if and only if for every space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+map"} projection map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon Y \times X \to Y
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
          %p
            In this article we will collect a number of proofs and points of view on this result, and show how it makes possible a very direct hands-on proof of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+theorem"} Tychonoff theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultrafilters"} ultrafilters
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
          %p
            The “only if” half is covered in essentially every textbook and should be routine for any working mathematician, although it seems proofs often use needlessly many indices and look as though they tacitly invoke the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          #onlyif.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+map"} projection map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon Y \times X \to Y
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subseteq Y \times X
              be a
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(C)
              is closed in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \notin \pi(C)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^{-1}(y) = \{y\} \times X
              does not intersect
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Topology+--+1#UnionOfOpensGivesClosure"} this lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighborhood"} open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              that does not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersect
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(C)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V \times X) \cap C = \emptyset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W \times U) \cap C = \emptyset
              for some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighborhood"} open neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} covers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y, x) \notin C
              for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and by closure of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              we can therefore find a neighborhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
